{
  "question": "Does buprenorphine need a PA?",
  "status": "answered",
  "assumption": "NY Medicaid (NYRx), since the program wasn't named and this is a coverage/PA question.",
  "answer": "Assuming NY Medicaid: **No PA for buprenorphine used for SUD** when prescribed per generally accepted national guidelines (PDL revised 9/14/2026, MAT Formulary).\n\n- Covered without PA: buprenorphine SL tablet, buprenorphine/naloxone tablet and film, Suboxone film, Zubsolv, plus Sublocade and Brixadi.\n- Quantity limits still apply. Buprenorphine SL: 8 tablets dispensed as a 2-day supply, max 32 mg/day. Buprenorphine/naloxone has its own limits, which I saw only in part, so check PDL p. 76.\n- If a PA is required for another drug, only the prescriber can request it. The pharmacist's only PA is the 72-hour emergency supply.\n\nThe documents don't address buprenorphine products for pain (e.g., patches) in what I retrieved.",
